You're creating a new object literal each render, so `props.obj` is a new reference every time and `React.memo`/shallow compare always fails.

```jsx
// parent re-renders → new object → child re-renders
<Child config={{ a: 1 }} />

// fix: stable reference
const config = useMemo(() => ({ a: 1 }), []);
<Child config={config} />   // + export default memo(Child)
```

Note: `memo` alone does nothing here — you need both the stable prop and the memoized child; same applies to inline callbacks (`useCallback`).

